# 16. When to Use Comprehensions

### Good use

```python
high_value = [
    transaction["amount"]
    for transaction in transactions
    if transaction["amount"] > 5000
]
```

Think:

```text
Collection
    ↓
Filter / Transform
    ↓
New Collection
```

### Use a normal loop when there are multiple actions

```python
for transaction in transactions:

    if not transaction["matched"]:
        log_issue(transaction)
        send_alert(transaction)
        create_ticket(transaction)
```

**Don't use comprehensions simply because they are shorter.**

Readability matters.

